    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds a complete Docusaurus v3 documentation website under `website/` with the following structure:\n\n### Getting Started\n- **Introduction** \u2014 what oap-bootstrap is and how it relates to OAP\n- **Prerequisites** \u2014 required tools, accounts, and tokens\n- **Quickstart** \u2014 build, init, and provision step-by-step\n- **Status and Scope** \u2014 current implementation status and non-goals\n\n### Concepts (How It Works)\n- **Phase Model** \u2014 the 7-phase dependency graph and idempotency guarantees\n- **Configuration and Provenance** \u2014 the 4-provenance model and fork seams\n- **Secrets at Rest** \u2014 SOPS/age encryption and the cleartext bridge lifecycle\n- **GitHub App and Identity** \u2014 App Manifest flow and Rauthy OIDC client creation\n\n### CLI Reference\n- **Commands Overview** \u2014 summary of the command surface\n- **Command Reference** \u2014 per-command flags and behavior\n\n### Operations\n- **Troubleshooting** \u2014 common issues and recovery steps\n\n### Project\n- **Governance** \u2014 spec-spine discipline and drift prevention\n\n## Build Verification\n\n```\nnpm run build   # exits 0, onBrokenLinks: throw\n```\n\n## Note on Workflow File\n\nThe `.github/workflows/deploy-docs.yml` file is prepared locally at `.github/workflows/deploy-docs.yml` but could not be pushed because the current GitHub App token lacks the `workflows` permission. It should be committed separately once the permission is granted, or pushed manually with a PAT that has the `workflow` scope.\n\nSpec-Drift-Waiver: no spec-owned code paths are modified; this PR adds documentation only.",
